    "continent": "Oceania",
    "notes_unique": "Smallest republic in world (21 km², 3rd smallest country after Vatican/Monaco); phosphate boom and bust (bird guano phosphate deposits mined from 1907, British Phosphate Commission then Nauru Phosphate Corporation, 1970s-80s highest per capita GDP on Earth ~$50k, Nauruans didn't have to work, invested in Melbourne real estate/London musicals/failed businesses, trust fund squandered, phosphate 80%+ exhausted by 2000s, interior of island is 'Topside' moonscape/coral pinnacles, 80% of land mined out, uninhabitable, environmental devastation, cautionary tale of resource curse); Australian offshore detention (2001 Pacific Solution, 2012 reopened, asylum seekers processed on Nauru, ~1,200 at peak, human rights abuses documented, mental health crisis, children detained, Amnesty/UNHCR condemnation, major revenue source for Nauru ~15-25% GDP, morally controversial); obesity epidemic (97% adults overweight, 71% obese, world's highest rates, Type 2 diabetes ~40%, imported processed food dependency, traditional fishing/gardening abandoned during phosphate wealth, public health crisis); WWII Japanese occupation (1942-45, 1,200 of 1,850 Nauruans deported to Truk/Chuuk, forced labour, 463 died, 2/3 population loss); no official capital (Yaren de facto, no cities, whole island is effectively one community); single oval road (island circumnavigation 19km); used as money laundering haven (1990s-2000s, 400+ shell banks, FATF blacklisted, international pariah, cleaned up); ICJ phosphate case (Nauru v Australia 1992, phosphate rehabilitation); parliament 19 members (one of smallest); weightlifting (disproportionate success at Commonwealth Games relative to population)",
